[h1]Rail Auto[/h1]
[b]Preview 0.1.1 · Gathering Storm single-player · Not verified in-game[/b]

Select a Military Engineer, Tycoon or another database-authorized railroad unit. Click the road icon in the standard bottom-right unit action row, then move normally. A selected icon means automatic rail laying is enabled; hover for status. Each unit has its own saved switch. Water and existing rails are skipped; construction resumes on eligible owned/unowned land.

Reads railroad prerequisites and base resource costs from the current database. Construction costs no extra movement and does not issue native build operations. Low resources disable construction while movement continues; replenish and resume manually. Rules that charge unit build charges are unsupported and pause construction. No free repair of pillaged rail, no promises for script/modifier costs or native construction climate/era-score side effects.

Targets Gathering Storm and HD v2.2. Game API behavior, per-tile events, UI, saves and current HD compatibility are unverified. Standard/Rise and Fall rulesets do not load the scripts. No multiplayer/hotseat. Avoid another rail automation on the same unit.

Author: xuanda0201. Original code and cover: MIT. Not an official release.
